# `.env` alone matches the exact name and nothing else, so `.env.bak`, `.env.old` and
# `.env.production` — the files people make while migrating secrets — were all committable to a
# PUBLIC repo. Ignore the whole family and re-admit the one file that is meant to be shared.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
data/

# Agent worktrees — separate checkouts of this repo, never part of it.
.claude/worktrees/
